# Hand-maintained Rust design doc, NOT a formatting target. Measured reasons, not preference:
#   1. prettier is NOT idempotent on it — it needed 4 --write passes to reach a fixed point, and
#      it oscillated on a blank line + a list-item indent in the middle of a >2-deep list.
#   2. The fixed point is LOSSY: reformatting glued inline code spans to adjacent words in 68
#      lines (e.g. "`…spawn()` on desktop" -> "`…spawn()`on desktop"), dropping the space.
# So running it would trade a format:check failure for 68 damaged lines of prose. Excluded
# rather than mangled; every other file in the repo stays fully checked.
